# Not read by the server at runtime — only bloats the build context that gets
# uploaded to Fly's remote builder on every deploy. docs/ alone is ~97MB;
# with node_modules and .git already excluded above, this was still the
# biggest thing left in the context (a first deploy took ~60 minutes,
# dominated by the COPY . . and export steps).
docs
study
chrome-extension
mac
windows
research
HANDOFF.md
TASKS.md
README.md

# Also never in the image, and the bulk of a local deploy's context: a local
# `fly deploy` from a working Mac checkout uploaded 2.3 GB, 2.2 GB of it data/.
# The final stage copies only package*.json, client/dist, server/ and scripts/,
# and the live database is the /data volume, so none of these can reach it.
# Patterns here are anchored at the repo root: `data` is the top-level data/,
# not server/data/, which the server reads and must stay.
data
analysis
test
# Local databases and their backups, wherever they sit: server/ and scripts/
# are copied into the image whole, so one left there would ship inside it.
# No .sqlite file is tracked in git.
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.bak
